rict leans R+6, most raters call it Lean or Likely R, and prediction markets give Democrats about a 30% chance. Democratic-sponsored polls show a close race and Lacore has outspent Honeycutt heavily, but the combined evidence still favors the GOP by a few points.", "watch": "A late influx of outside spending or another Democratic-leaning poll confirming a genuine tie would move this toward Tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Nancy Mace (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Nancy Mace's retirement leaves this Lowcountry seat open, and both parties see a real opportunity. Republican Jenny Costa Honeycutt and Democrat Nancy Lacore have traded attacks over experience, healthcare costs, and the Iran war in a well-covered October debate. The district's partisan lean favors Republicans, but a strong Democratic national environment keeps the race competitive.\n\nPolling is sparse and split by sponsor: Democratic-leaning surveys show Lacore tied or ahead, while a Republican-leaning poll shows Honeycutt up six. Lacore has raised far more money, though outside groups have boosted Honeycutt. Most expert ratings sit at Lean or Likely Republican, and prediction markets price a Republican win near 70%, making this a competitive but Republican-tilted race.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2812, "margin": -3.39}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2869, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2863, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.3426, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2352, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2308, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2761, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.3368, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2774, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2992, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.2787, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.3431, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-